  "screening": "Per-stream title/metadata retrieval and eligibility rules in search audits. Final merge removes missing identifiers/URLs, obvious withdrawn/non-research headings and out-of-scope applications. Priority tags are deterministic title signals: R1 manipulator/wrist/assembly and force/torque measurement + calibration/estimation; R2 robot/actuator and identification, saturation or reference-governor; R5 explicit mobile/multi-robot, cooperative localization or formation context + timing, delay, loss or intermittent communication. A missing tag can be a false negative. No inference of method efficacy from tags. Bibliographic types come from provider metadata. Exact calendar-day eligibility is not known for records containing only year.",
  "identity_rule": "Merge on equal normalized DOI, arXiv family, exact URL or normalized title and matching first author string. Distinct publication DOIs are kept unless a relationship was separately confirmed. Unresolved equal titles flagged. Preprint and publisher versions can still be distinct. baseline matched_identifier uses DOI/arXiv/URL; title-only matches are uncertain, remaining entries are unmatched in the checked snapshot only.",
